# The repository was written on Windows and every file landed in the index with
# CRLF. Rust and TypeScript tolerate that, but a shell script does not: bash
# reads the trailing \r as part of the command and dies on the first line, so
# install.sh and every contrib/ script were unrunnable on Linux and macOS.
#
# Normalise the index to LF and keep it that way. Windows checkouts are
# unaffected: git converts on checkout according to core.autocrlf there.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Scripts must be LF wherever they are checked out — a Windows clone that runs
# them under Git Bash or WSL hits the same failure otherwise.
*.sh text eol=lf

# PowerShell is the one place CRLF is the native convention.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
